    "donar_goal_tag": "Current Campaign",
    "donar_goal_title": "Seeking an industrial oven for our baking workshops",
    "donar_goal_desc": "We are seeking financial backing for our adult education project. With an industrial gas oven, participants in our baking classes will be able to produce bread for themselves and sell goods in the community, taking another step toward self-reliance.",
    "proyectos_hero_title": "Our Projects",
    "proj_01_title": "\"Santa Dorotea\" Children's Home",
    "proj_01_desc": "In our children's home, around 20 children and young people with various disabilities from rural Cajamarca are currently cared for. Some have been abandoned by their families and reside permanently; others stay during the week and return to their families on weekends and holidays. All residents attend the local special school, are taught in inclusion classes, or work in nearby enterprises, participating in numerous activities and workshops.",
    "proj_02_title": "Daytime Workshops at the Home",
    "proj_02_desc": "In our daytime courses, newly established in early 2023, around 50 young people and young adults from outside the home are attended daily. This is a private social and educational program funded by our association. Participants learn Braille for the visually impaired, sewing, theater, dance, cooking and baking, table manners, and daily tasks such as gardening and cleaning.",
    "proj_03_title": "Jesús Rehabilitation Center",
    "proj_03_desc": "In the town of Jesús, we run a rehabilitation center supporting 25 children with disabilities. In partnership with the local municipality, we offer specialized therapies and tailored learning to empower them with everyday independence and social participation.",
    "proj_04_title": "\"El Porongo\" Ecological Farm",
    "proj_04_desc": "At our \"El Porongo\" farm, homes and apartments were built and are largely rented out to generate sustainable income for the association. It hosts the apartment for our annual German volunteers and has future plans for housing former students and seniors, while serving as an educational excursion site for local schools with animal care and farm experience.",
    "proj_05_title": "CEEC Special Education School",
    "proj_05_desc": "In close partnership with the CEEC special school, we provide qualified special education for students with intellectual, motor, and sensory disabilities, supporting student transport and funding essential staff members.",
    "proj_06_title": "Audiometry Department",
    "proj_06_desc": "Two Peruvian staff members alongside volunteer German audiologists perform hearing tests and fit donated hearing aids, making hearing care accessible for underprivileged families in Cajamarca.",
    "proj_07_title": "Medical Campaigns",
    "proj_07_desc": "We regularly organize medical missions with volunteer local and international doctors, providing corrective surgeries for cleft lip and palate, dental treatments, and general healthcare for disadvantaged families.",
    "proj_08_title": "Social Support & Scholarships",
    "proj_08_desc": "Our social program assists vulnerable families facing medical hardships by covering clinical expenses and awarding scholarships to deserving students who would otherwise lack educational opportunities.",
    "proj_09_title": "Casa Cuba in Lima",
    "proj_09_desc": "A shelter home in Lima providing lodging and compassionate support for patients and their accompanying relatives who must travel from Cajamarca for specialized medical care in the capital.",
    "proj_10_title": "\"Los Jazmines\" Guesthouse & Café",
    "proj_10_desc": "Acquired with the help of Caritas Germany, this charming colonial guesthouse and café in central Cajamarca provides meaningful employment for people with disabilities. Offering 15 rooms, a garden, and a terrace (also hosting free sign language classes), it generates independent funds to sustain our charitable mission.",
    "nosotros_hero_title": "About Us",
    "nosotros_history_title": "Our History",
    "nosotros_history_p1": "Since 1976, a project dedicated to the education, care, and rehabilitation of children and young people with disabilities has existed in Cajamarca. First, a special education school (Centro de Educación Especial) was established, followed by the founding of a children's home to accommodate students with disabilities and orphans from the rural areas of Cajamarca.",
    "nosotros_history_p2": "Simultaneously, workshops and a school farm were created. Because specialized medical care is often lacking in Cajamarca, many patients must travel to the capital city of Lima. For their lodging and care, the project provides a shelter home in Lima (Casa Cuba). With the support of Caritas Germany, a property in the center of Cajamarca was acquired, now housing a small hotel and cafe (Los Jazmines), where individuals with disabilities find employment opportunities and which provides independent income for the association.",
    "nosotros_history_p3": "The governing body is the Asociación Santa Dorotea, chaired by Christa Stark, supported by committed educational and healthcare specialists.",
    "nosotros_founder_title": "Our Founder",
    "nosotros_founder_role": "Founder",
    "nosotros_founder_bio": "Christa Stark was born on December 12, 1943, in Pomerania. She grew up in Nordfriesland as a pastor's daughter and studied Special Education in Hamburg and Dortmund. In 1975, she arrived in Peru through the German Development Service (DED). Shortly after, she reached Cajamarca, founded the special school, and established the children's home in 1990 to provide shelter to children from remote Andean provinces.",
